  "term": "vertigo",
  "definition": "Vertigo is a false sense of movement, such as feeling that you are spinning or that the surroundings are spinning around you. It can occur in connection with problems affecting the inner ear, vestibular nerve, brainstem, or cerebral cortex, and may also appear during some focal seizures.",
